*---------------------------------------------------------------
* mli.equ -- ProDOS 8 MLI parameter-list shapes and field VALUES
* that liba's file calls need, transcribed VERBATIM from the
* ProDOS 8 Technical Reference Manual ch. 4 (housekeeping/filing
* calls) and Appendix B.4.2 (access/storage_type/file_type
* attributes) -- fetched live this round from the TRM artifact
* cited by learning:01KW1GTYGP8MHN9YAE5JTSP62Z, not from memory.
* docs/SYSCALL.md ruling 3 requires file-call parmlists to be
* the REAL MLI shapes, verbatim -- this file (plus each util's
* own static parmlist declarations, which use these shapes
* directly via `dfb`/`da` rather than an indirected `dum`/`dend`
* offset table, since each util needs exactly ONE instance per
* call type, not an array) is where that verbatim shape is
* recorded once so five utils don't independently transcribe it
* and risk five independent transcription slips.
* Full design notes: L.MLIE.TXT (docs/a2/)
*---------------------------------------------------------------

PCOUNT_CREATE   equ   7

* See L.MLIE.TXT: "DESTROY ($C1) -- TRM 4.4.2 3"
PCNT_DESTROY  equ   1

* See L.MLIE.TXT: "OPEN ($C8) -- TRM 4.5.1 6"
PCOUNT_OPEN     equ   3

* See L.MLIE.TXT: "READ ($CA) -- TRM 4.5.3 8"
PCOUNT_READ     equ   4

* See L.MLIE.TXT: "WRITE ($CB) -- TRM 4.5.4 8"
PCOUNT_WRITE    equ   4

* See L.MLIE.TXT: "CLOSE ($CC) -- TRM 4.5.5 3"
PCOUNT_CLOSE    equ   1
PCNT_RENAME     equ   2        ;pathname + new_pathname

* -- GET_FILE_INFO ($C4) -- TRM 4.4.3, param_count $0A (10):
* -- pathname ptr, access, file_type, aux_type(2), storage_type,
* -- blocks_used(2), mod_date(2), mod_time(2), create_date(2),
* -- create_time(2). Added 2026-08-19 (task: wire GET_FILE_INFO
* -- into the kernel broker + liba) -- transcribed from the same
* -- TRM artifact the rest of this file cites, not from memory.
PCOUNT_GFI      equ   10

* -- SET_FILE_INFO ($C3) -- TRM 4.4.4, param_count 7: pathname
* -- ptr, access, file_type, aux_type(2), null_field(3 bytes --
* -- TRM: "preserve symmetry between this and the GET_FILE_INFO
* -- call", should be zero), mod_date(2), mod_time(2). No
* -- storage_type/blocks_used/create_date/create_time slots --
* -- those are not settable via this call. Added 2026-08-21
* -- (chmod task): read-modify-write is the CALLER's job (GET_
* -- FILE_INFO first, change only access, write file_type/
* -- aux_type/dates back unchanged) -- see src/bin/chmod.s.
PCOUNT_SFI      equ   7

* ---- pathname buffer shape (used by OPEN/CREATE/DESTROY's
* pathname ---- pointer field, TRM 4.4.1/4.5.1 prose): 1-byte
* COUNT, then up to 64 ---- RAW 7-BIT-ASCII characters -- NOT
* NUL-terminated, NOT high-bit-set. ---- "ProDOS clears this
* high bit" (TRM ch. 2, "By the Way" note on ---- Apple II ASCII
* convention) -- liba's own high-bit-set string ---- convention
* (docs/USERLAND.md) is backwards from what the MLI wants, ----
* so src/liba/mli.s's MKPATH is a MANDATORY boundary conversion,
* not ---- a nicety. See docs/USERLAND.md "ABI RESOLUTIONS" for
* the citation.
MLI_PTH_MAXLN equ   64

* See L.MLIE.TXT: "CREATE field VALUES this round had"
ACCESS_UNLKD equ   $C3
* -- access byte bit masks (TRM 4.4.3 -- "D RN B rsv rsv rsv W
* -- R", bits 7 6 5 4-2 1 0). docs/ANACHRONISMS.md sec W2 rules
* -- OUT a Unix rwx mapping -- chmod.s speaks these bits
* -- directly, letters d/n/b/w/r (learning:01M0798FFCHB60SW-
* -- QDE8NQEQXN, the GNO/ME precedent). Bits 4-2 are reserved;
* -- "only ProDOS may change" them (TRM) -- chmod never touches
* -- them.
ACC_DESTROY equ   $80
ACC_RENAME  equ   $40
ACC_BACKUP  equ   $20
ACC_WRITE   equ   $02
ACC_READ    equ   $01
* See L.MLIE.TXT: "filetype ($06  BIN) standard ProDOS"
FTYPE_BIN       equ   $06
* -- The type is maux's OWN metadata, not an interop
* -- courtesy. It is where "can this be run?" lives (the GNO
* -- precedent: no chmod +x, use chtyp), what Merlin filters
* -- on when self-hosting, and what ls -l will report.
* -- Creating everything BIN, as this tree did until
* -- 2026-08-17, throws all three away silently.
FTYPE_TXT       equ   $04        ;ProDOS TXT. What a shell
                                 ;redirect and an ed write
                                 ;produce -- both are text
                                 ;streams by definition
* See L.MLIE.TXT: "storagetype ($01  seedling) TRM Appendix"
STYP_SEEDLING  equ   $01
STYP_DIR        equ   $0D        ;storage_type for a directory
FTYPE_DIR       equ   $0F        ;file_type DIR. CREATE makes a
                                 ;real subdirectory when both
                                 ;are set -- which is why mkdir
                                 ;needs no kernel support

* -- the rest of Appendix B.4.2's file_type byte values.
* -- Identity mapping only (which byte means what) --
* -- RENDERING (a 3-char ls column vs. file's prose) stays
* -- per-tool, docs/PLAN.md "The liba wave".
FTYPE_SYS       equ   $FF        ;system program
FTYPE_BAS       equ   $FC        ;applesoft program
FTYPE_INT       equ   $FA        ;integer basic program
FTYPE_VAR       equ   $FB        ;applesoft variables
FTYPE_REL       equ   $FE        ;REGISTERED relocatable code
                                 ;-- Apple's own EDASM toolchain
                                 ;(ESD/RLD records) -- NOT the
                                 ;Merlin format (FTYPE_RELM).
FTYPE_RELM      equ   $F8        ;MERLIN REL object -- NOT $FE:
                                 ;real Merlin-8 writes its REL
                                 ;modules (code + dictionary,
                                 ;aux = code length) as $F8,
                                 ;measured off five real files
                                 ;(docs/REL-LIBA-SPIKE.md). $FE
                                 ;is the EDASM convention and no
                                 ;maux tool reads or writes it.
FTYPE_PAS       equ   $EF        ;pascal area
FTYPE_ATK       equ   $E2        ;appletalk file
FTYPE_S16       equ   $B3        ;gs/os application
